                <pb facs="0331" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.84/72: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Addis Ababa</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cramp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-06T01:00:00+03:00">May 6, 1936—1 a.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 5—8:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>293. Italian headquarters at palace have sent me captain, lieutenant, and 50 men.
                    Have had them placed outside Legation compound. They inform me nearest occupying
                    force 6¼ miles away. Also that between 25 and 30 thousand Italians here so that
                    by morning the situation will be entirely under control. The city is now calm
                    with only an occasional shot.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cramp</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
